{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>May HaShem affix</b>, etc. This punishment and the curses stated until ״and you shall be a tail״ — they correspond to the nullification of negative commandments (לא תעשה), and therefore Scripture concludes: <b>and all these curses shall come upon you</b>, etc., <b>because you did not heed the voice of HaShem to keep His commandments</b> — see then that the curses stated in this passage are on account of nullifying negative commandments. The discerning one will understand, regarding all the curses, that they are evils drawn from transgressions. And its saying <b>May HaShem affix to you</b>, etc. — because one who transgresses even a single transgression acquires for himself an evil portion that becomes affixed to his soul to defile it, and this is the sod of the maladies of the soul, as is known. And the evil portion is called dever (pestilence), in the manner that the sages of blessed memory said (Tosafot, Shabbat 89a, s.v. Torah) regarding the verse (Habakkuk 3:5): ״לְפָנָיו יֵלֶךְ דָּבֶר״ — that דָּבֶר alludes to the Samekh-Mem the wicked, who is called dever. And it is known that all the forces of evil are branches of the Samekh-Mem and are called by his name. Also the curse of consumption and fever, etc. — they are things brought about by transgressions, in the manner of their statement in the Gemara (Shabbat 55a): Rabbi Ami said, there is no death without sin and no suffering without iniquity, for iniquity gives birth to diseases in the body, as it says (Jeremiah 2:19): ״תְּיַסְּרֵךְ רָעָתֵךְ״, etc." "And likewise its saying <b>and your heavens shall be</b>, etc. — in the manner of their statement of blessed memory (Zohar 1:6a) that through the interposition of transgressions the channels of influence are shut off, in the sod of (Job 14:11): ״וְנָהָר יֶחֱרַב וְיָבֵשׁ״." "And likewise its saying <b>HaShem shall strike you with a plague</b>, etc. — this too transgressions bring about, as hinted in the verse (Ecclesiastes 8:9): ״אֲשֶׁר יִשְׁלֹט הָאָדָם בְּאָדָם לְרַע לוֹ״ — meaning, because of the evil that is attached to him, as hinted in the phrase ״יַדְבֵּק ה׳ בְּךָ אֶת הַדָּבֶר״, and so all the curses stated in this passage are brought about by the practice of evil." "And its saying <b>״and they shall be in you for a sign and for a wonder״</b> (Deuteronomy 28:46) — for one who transgresses a single transgression, it is inscribed upon his forehead." "And its saying <b>and in your seed forever.</b> For the evil soul of a person — by virtue of the portions of impurity attached to it, as we have said — the children it produces will be like itself, as we explained this matter thoroughly in parashat Vayechi at the verse ״רְאוּבֵן בְכוֹרִי אַתָּה״ (Genesis 49:3). This too is the sod of the death decreed upon man and upon all generations coming from him, for the reason that all who proceed from him tasted death through his sin, and this is the sod of man's orlah (foreskin). Therefore it says <b>and in your seed forever</b>, for when the evil portion is affixed to a person it will be passed down from one to the next forever, and it requires enormous strength to cleanse it from his soul."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:50.144204556Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}